Z||000008||Cliff Pennock||10-29-2000||05:16 AM||||(Reposted under correct username)<P>LOL@TB!<P>BatBoy, my C566 is also happily running @ 850 without the need for extra cooling. I can definitely recommend the Microsoft FF joystick - not the new version but the old one. The new version sucks big time in the opinion of most users. I like the old one very much. This might very well be the only good product Microsoft has ever made.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I would also suggest getting yourself a FF steering wheel. You'll love racing with it. I would recommend the Logitech FF Wheel - again the old version - not the new.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Predator||10-29-2000||07:04 AM||||If anybody is interested I have a home network setup with 6 PC's. All share a cable modem using a Linksys 4 port Router. I have a Linksys print server and a couple of hubs to put everything together. I have 2 teenagers so they have 2 upstairs in their room, and I have a PIII 600 for me. I have 2 PC's running Linux which I use to run my email and a small website. It is fun to play with. ANyway I thought I would throw my 2 cents worth in. Happy Computing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
